//
// LLAMA-3.2-3B BF16 prefill TTFT vs padded prefill length, into
// llama32_3b.prefill_sweep.json (collected by the nightly LLM benchmark).
//
// The bf16 models used to publish a single scalar TTFT while the q4nx ones
// published a curve, which put the two families in separate tables. Nothing in
// this design fixes the length: compile_all_kernels() is parameterized by
// seq_len and picks its GEMM herd_m and FlashAttention tiling from it. What
// fixed the length was a hardcoded `seq_len = 2048` in build_session, now the
// CTX make variable.
//
// The axis is the PADDED length, not the prompt length: the prompt is padded to
// the built length and the last real token's row is read, so at a fixed engine
// TTFT does not move with the prompt. Every point therefore rebuilds the
// engines, into a per-CTX cache directory -- KernelCache keys entries on kernel
// name alone, so sharing one directory across lengths would silently time the
// previous length's ELFs. sweep_prefill.py independently guards that by reading
// the built length off the "Compiling prefill kernels (seq_len=N)" line.
//
// Latency only, never a correctness gate (run_npu2_verify.lit is that). Needs
// real weights, because a prefill is a prefill.
//
// Measured on a Ryzen AI 9 HX 370: 692 / 1267 / 2735 / 6422 ms at
// 512 / 1024 / 2048 / 4096.
//
// 4096 was left out of an earlier revision of this file on the theory that its
// f32 GEMM scratch would push a 64GB runner over, next to a verify phase that
// already measures ~24GB. It was never measured. It fits, so it is swept.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, hf_token, hfweights_meta_llama_llama_3_2_3b_instruct
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_peano_prefill_sweep
// RUN: cd test_peano_prefill_sweep
// RUN: %PYTHON %S/../bench/sweep_prefill.py --model-name llama32_3b --makefile %S/Makefile --lengths 512,1024,2048,4096 --seq-env LLM_SEQ_LEN --bench-env LLM_BENCH_L --peano-dir %PEANO_INSTALL_DIR --out llama32_3b.prefill_sweep.json
// RUN: FileCheck %s < llama32_3b.prefill_sweep.json
// CHECK: "model": "llama32_3b"
// CHECK: "axis": "prefill_len"
// A parsed number at the reference length, not just a well-formed file: if the
// driver's TTFT line drifts out of sweep_prefill.py's regex every point goes
// null and the published curve silently empties while the test stays green.
// CHECK: "prefill_len": 2048
// CHECK-NEXT: "ttft_ms": {{[0-9]}}
